course: dictionary
lesson: 2130
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which meaning the writer wants. The word here is cooker. «A girl in Leeds left a pan handle sticking out over the edge of the cooker.» A pan sits on a cooker, and the pan handle is near the hot part, so cooker must mean the big kitchen machine with an oven and hot plates.
explain: «A pressure cooker traps steam so the pressure rises.» The word before cooker, pressure, is a clue. Pressure cooker is one kind of machine that cooks food, so cooker can mean any machine for cooking. Notice how the first word in a phrase can narrow down the meaning of the second.
explain: Context also tells you what something is for. «It has a safety valve and only grown-ups use it.» A machine with a safety valve is dangerous to use without care, so it is probably a cooker that gets very hot. Ask yourself: what word would fit here, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A word can have several meanings, and the sentence shows which one is meant.
fact: «Cooker» can mean a large kitchen machine with an oven and hot plates, which is called a stove in the USA.
fact: «Cooker» can also mean any machine for cooking, such as a «slow cooker» or a «rice cooker».
fact: «Cooker» can mean an apple meant for cooking rather than eating raw. This is informal British use.
exercise: «A toddler in Ohio pulled on a saucepan handle sticking out over the edge of the cooker.» What is the cooker in this sentence? | *A kitchen machine with an oven and hot plates | A bed | A type of tree | A pair of shoes
exercise: «A pressure cooker traps steam so the pressure rises and water boils at a higher temperature.» What does cooker mean here? | A kind of kitchen window | A stove in the USA only | *Any machine for cooking food | An apple for cooking
exercise: Which words in «Hot drinks and pans pulled from the edge of tables and cookers are a common cause of serious burns in small children» tell you the danger? | common | serious | children | *burns
test: «A carbon monoxide alarm senses carbon monoxide, a poison gas that can come from badly burning boilers, fires or cookers.» What does cookers mean in this sentence? | *Machines for cooking that can burn fuel badly | Cookers that rise in price | Cooks who work in restaurants | Biscuits baked at home
test: Why does the word «pressure» help you understand «pressure cooker»? | It shows the cooker is a type of cooking machine, so cooker means any machine for cooking | *It has nothing to do with the meaning, so ignore it | It means the cooker is cold | It shows the cooker is sold in shops
exam: «Drinks pulled from the edge of a cooker are a common cause of serious burns.» What is the best meaning of cooker here? | *A large kitchen machine with an oven and hot plates | A person who cooks dinner | An apple for eating raw | A pan with a lid
